"""Hand-listed mutants of the two regenerated bindings of the observable container spec (examples/qt/spec_regen).

Each mutant is one textual edit of one header, written so that the tree still compiles under -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic
(an edit that leaves a variable or parameter unused keeps it used with a cast to void). A mutant is KILLED when the binding's own ctest
fails, SURVIVES when it passes, and is NOT VIABLE when the tree does not build (a mutant that is not viable is rewritten, never
counted). A mutant that survives is either killed by a test added to the binding, or judged equivalent, with the reason, in
EQUIVALENT below.

  (name, file under the binding, old text, new text, constraint)

`constraint` is true for an edit that only the compile-fail tests (AT-9.n) can see; the runtime tests are run first and the
compile-fail ones only for those.
"""

# The two bindings share the design and differ in the spelling of a signal (binding A emits QVariant keys, binding B calls a typed
# signal), so each list is written out in full.

